  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Norarecoline and U373 MG, a cancer cell line, through a series of molecular interactions. Norarecoline is implicated in targeting Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9, which is a key enzyme involved in the metabolism of certain steroids. This enzyme is further targeted by a complex steroid molecule, which in turn has a direct effect on U373 MG cells. The evidence indicates that Norarecoline may modulate the activity of this enzyme, potentially influencing the cellular processes that drive the growth and survival of U373 MG. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but the exact mechanism by which Norarecoline affects U373 MG remains to be fully elucidated. The pathways highlight a possible role of SDR family members in mediating the effects of Norarecoline on cancer cells, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm these findings."
